  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.54,
      "end_seconds": 3.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "hello good to see you please sit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.87,
      "end_seconds": 5.77,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "hello doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.23,
      "end_seconds": 10.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.86,
      "end_seconds": 17.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "so so the thing is, I've got a blister on my heel"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.57,
      "end_seconds": 21.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.77,
      "end_seconds": 25.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "about... well, six months"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.75,
      "end_seconds": 36.62,
      "duration_seconds": 9.87,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets how often and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.95,
      "end_seconds": 53.84,
      "duration_seconds": 15.89,
      "text": "A plaster helps a bit. It's worse with new shoes. I've been putting this off for weeks. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.59,
      "end_seconds": 58.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Right, does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.12,
      "end_seconds": 72.25,
      "duration_seconds": 13.13,
      "text": "it usually comes with a little soreness. Erm the the little soreness? That's been for one week. With little soreness walking definitely sets it off"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.38,
      "end_seconds": 91.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "tell me about your routine work habits that sort of thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.92,
      "end_seconds": 108.45,
      "duration_seconds": 11.53,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. My partner and our baby. I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.0,
      "end_seconds": 113.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "any allergies to tablets food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.28,
      "end_seconds": 120.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Plasters. I come out in... well, a red itchy rash"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.16,
      "end_seconds": 124.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.17,
      "end_seconds": 130.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "I've had high cholesterol for about ten years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.26,
      "end_seconds": 135.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "right, and and anything else to add?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.0,
      "end_seconds": 141.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for about ten years now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.26,
      "end_seconds": 149.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "alright high cholesterol that that matches what I have here let's run through your medicines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.09,
      "end_seconds": 158.26,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "Simvastatin 20 milligrams at night. I take metformin 500 milligrams twice a day for my sugar"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.59,
      "end_seconds": 160.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "How about fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.78,
      "end_seconds": 164.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Ah, no, none, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.52,
      "end_seconds": 168.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Have you noticed pus or redness spreading?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.75,
      "end_seconds": 172.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "No, no pus or redness spreading."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.58,
      "end_seconds": 178.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.55,
      "end_seconds": 182.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 199.49,
      "end_seconds": 207.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "here are the numbers, doctor heart rate 74, BP is 113 over 74, oxygen saturation is 98 percent"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.37,
      "end_seconds": 210.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "good, thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.59,
      "end_seconds": 214.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.26,
      "end_seconds": 218.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "hold that for a second"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.09,
      "end_seconds": 239.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "It's an intact blister on the back of the heel with no redness around it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.78,
      "end_seconds": 258.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.01,
      "end_seconds": 272.27,
      "duration_seconds": 11.26,
      "text": "so, that's all I needed to to check so, based on the history and the examination, I think we're dealing with a simple friction blister at this stage"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.3,
      "end_seconds": 277.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.7,
      "end_seconds": 289.83,
      "duration_seconds": 10.13,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the the moment I'd say it's a simple friction blister and we'll watch how it goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.01,
      "end_seconds": 325.08,
      "duration_seconds": 26.07,
      "text": "Leave it intact, cover it with a padded plaster and change the shoes. Keep an eye out, and if the area becomes red, hot or pus-filled, call us the the same day or go to emergency. I'd like you back if it looks infected. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.04,
      "end_seconds": 330.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}